---
title: Sign in with Nostr
description: Sign in to the campus with no password or email, by signing with your Nostr identity from a browser extension.
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

If you have a Nostr identity (an `npub`), you can enter the campus with one click. Your extension signs a challenge and the campus verifies the signature. **Your private key never leaves your browser**: the server only ever sees your public key.

## What you need

A browser extension that supports NIP-07. The most common ones:

- [Alby](https://getalby.com/) (Chrome, Firefox, Brave)
- [nos2x](https://github.com/fiatjaf/nos2x) (Chrome, Brave) or [nos2x-fox](https://diegogurpegui.com/nos2x-fox/) (Firefox)
- Flamingo, Nostore and other NIP-07 compatible extensions

{% aside type="caution" title="Mobile" %}
Browser extensions do not work in most mobile browsers. On your phone, use [GitHub or Google](/en/acceso/login-github-google/), or the [username and password](/en/acceso/crear-cuenta/) of your account.
{% /aside %}

## Steps

{% steps %}

1. Install the extension and create or import your Nostr key following the extension's own instructions.

2. Open [campus.ismos.xyz/login](https://campus.ismos.xyz/login/index.php) and click **⚡ Log in with Nostr**, the purple button below the username and password form. It takes a couple of seconds to appear.

3. The extension will ask permission to share your **public key**. Accept.

4. It will then ask you to **sign** the login request. Accept as well. You are signing a single-use event that expires in two minutes; it is not a transaction and authorises nothing else.

5. Within a few seconds you are on your Dashboard.

{% /steps %}

## The first time

The first sign-in with a Nostr key creates your account automatically:

- **Display name**: taken from your Nostr profile (the `display_name` in your profile event). If you have no published profile, a generic name is used, which you can change in [your profile](/en/cuenta/perfil-e-idioma/).
- **Email**: you are never asked for one. The campus generates a placeholder address from your `npub`. See below for what that means.

## You will not receive any email

To protect your privacy, signing in with Nostr **never asks you for an email**: the campus builds a placeholder address from your `npub`. That address does not exist, so:

- **You will receive no email or communication from the campus**: no course notices, no forum replies, no assignment reminders, no announcements.
- Your identity stays unlinked to a real email address, which is the whole point.

This is the default behaviour and for many people it is the desired one. But if you were expecting notices and nothing arrives, this is why — it is not a fault.

### If you do want them

You have to **manually replace** that placeholder with your real address in [your campus profile](/en/cuenta/perfil-e-idioma/): avatar → **Profile** → **Edit profile** → **Email address**. You will get a confirmation email at the new address.

{% aside type="caution" title="It is a trade-off" %}
The moment you enter a real email, your campus account is tied to it. If you chose Nostr precisely to avoid that, leave the placeholder alone and read your notices inside the campus, under **Preferences → Notification preferences**.
{% /aside %}

### A middle path: an address that isn't your everyday one

You don't have to choose between receiving nothing and handing over your personal address. You can use one that receives mail but isn't tied to your identity:

- **A new account with a privacy-focused provider.** [Proton Mail](https://proton.me/mail) and [Tuta](https://tuta.com/) (formerly Tutanota) have free plans, ask for no personal details and encrypt the mailbox. Create one just for the campus.
- **An alias that forwards to your usual inbox.** You give the campus a different address and the mail arrives where you already read it: [SimpleLogin](https://simplelogin.io/), [addy.io](https://addy.io/) or [DuckDuckGo Email Protection](https://duckduckgo.com/email/). If it ever becomes a nuisance, you switch the alias off and that's that — your account is untouched.

Either way you get the campus notices and your personal address never shows up anywhere.

{% aside type="note" title="On the roadmap" %}
Building a Nostr-based communication system inside Moodle is on our roadmap, so that Nostr accounts can receive campus notices without giving up privacy or handing over an email address. Until then, the two options above are what you have.
{% /aside %}

## Common errors

| Message | Meaning | What to do |
| --- | --- | --- |
| *No Nostr extension found* | The browser has no active NIP-07 extension | Install Alby or nos2x and reload the page |
| *Extension denied access* | You declined to share the public key | Try again and accept the permission in the extension |
| *Signing cancelled* | You declined to sign the request | Try again and accept the signature |
| *Could not fetch login challenge* | The page had been open too long | Reload the page and try again |
| *Network error* | No connection, or the relay is not responding | Check your connection and retry |

## Privacy and security

- The campus receives only your public key and a signature. It cannot post on your behalf or read your messages.
- The signature covers a unique challenge that includes the campus URL, so it cannot be replayed elsewhere.
- The plugin behind this login is free software built by Librería de Satoshi: [moodle-auth_nostr on GitHub](https://github.com/LibreriadeSatoshi/moodle-auth_nostr).
